# Backend startup guard

After any backend change (routes, controllers, services, models, imports, API):

1. Imports - verify paths, exports, ESM, case-sensitive filenames.
2. Start - run npm run dev in backend/ until no crash. Do **not** start a second backend in another terminal/background (causes EADDRINUSE on 5000). Reuse an already-running instance when healthy.
3. Health - GET /api/v1/health (default port 5000).
4. Do not finish with a crashed backend.
5. `npm run dev:safe` (project root) or `npm run dev` (backend/) runs `dev-preflight.cjs` first — clears duplicate **CRM Node** on PORT 5000/4000 only.

Report: files changed, startup result, APIs checked, errors fixed.

See CURSOR_SAFE_CHANGE_RULES.md Backend safety section.